Third-party rules and materials
------------------------------

The MIT license above covers this project's original contributions. It does
not replace the licenses of attributed third-party rules, images, or other
materials. See docs/sources.md and the relevant source and asset notes.

book/34-shared-stories.md, docs/evidence/F32-action-and-consequences.md,
and docs/evidence/F65-clocks-and-flashbacks.md
include Chinese paraphrases and adaptations of selected Blades in the Dark
SRD rules. The fictional examples and probability calculations are original
to this project. No game setting, artwork, maps, or logos are reproduced.

This work is based on Blades in the Dark (found at http://www.bladesinthedark.com/), product of One Seven Design, developed and authored by John Harper, and licensed for our use under the Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 Unported license (http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/).

book/34-shared-stories.md and docs/evidence/F33-aspects-and-shared-fiction.md
include Chinese paraphrases and adaptations of selected Fate Condensed
official SRD text. Fate Condensed (c) 2020 Evil Hat Productions, LLC.
The fictional examples and value arguments are original to this project.

This work is based on Fate Condensed (found at http://www.faterpg.com/), a product of Evil Hat Productions, LLC, developed, authored, and edited by PK Sullivan, Lara Turner, Leonard Balsera, Fred Hicks, Richard Bellingham, Robert Hanz, Ryan Macklin, and Sophie Lagacé, and licensed for our use under the Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 Unported license (http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/).

These adaptations are not official translations. Neither rights holder has
reviewed, endorsed, or sponsored this project. No trademark or logo license
is implied by the project's MIT license.

book/15-neighborhood.md and docs/evidence/F35-public-life-observation.md
include limited Chinese paraphrases, abridgments and reorganizations of
selected Public Life Data Protocol companion survey methods, licensed
under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
Source: https://github.com/gehl-institute/pldp/tree/1b051183e1764338b4823556922747c610e1d8de

The Public Life Data Protocol was jointly developed by Gehl Institute, Gehl, the City of Copenhagen, The City of San Francisco, and Seattle Department of Transportation.

The fictional examples, arithmetic and value arguments are this project's
original contributions. These method explanations are not an official
translation. No survey layout, icon or sample personal data is reproduced.
The institutions have not reviewed, sponsored or endorsed this project.

assets/media/pocket-met-157045.jpg is a resized, JPEG-encoded public-domain
collection image supplied by The Metropolitan Museum of Art Open Access API:
Pocket, American, ca. 1784, accession 2009.300.2241, object ID 157045.
Brooklyn Museum Costume Collection at The Metropolitan Museum of Art,
Gift of the Brooklyn Museum, 2009; Bequest of Marie Bernice Bitzer,
by exchange, 1996.
The object-level public-domain flag and API image documentation are recorded
in docs/evidence/F66-pockets-and-dress.md and assets/media/README.md.
This image is not an original MIT-licensed artwork by this project.
No V&A images or logos are reproduced. No museum endorsement is implied.
